<section class="text text--content-callout aem-GridColumn aem-GridColumn--default--12">
<div id="content-callout-box-c96f82b0ed" class="cmp-text">
    <h3><b>2024 NAEP Math Scores Decline Since 2019; 4th Grade Math Scores Increase Since 2022.</b></h3>
<ul>
<li>Math scores in 4th grade increased by 2 points nationally, largely driven by higher-performing students, compared to 2022.</li>
<li>Math scores in 8th grade had the largest decline ever in 2022, though scores did not change significantly in 2024. </li>
<li>The 2024 average 12th grade math score is down 3 points from 2019 and is the lowest score ever reported for 12th grade. Forty-five percent of students are working below <i>NAEP Basic</i> – the highest percentage ever.</li>
</ul>

</div>

    

</section>
